 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 00. Environment Setup and First Spark Run\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook helps you prepare your local environment for PySpark learning. We will install dependencies, validate Java and Python, and run a first simple Spark job.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Goals\n",
    "- Confirm Python and Java are available\n",
    "- Install PySpark and notebook dependencies\n",
    "- Run a simple distributed job\n",
    "- Understand the SparkSession entry point\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys\n",
    "import platform\n",
    "print('Python version:', sys.version)\n",
    "print('Platform:', platform.platform())\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Verify Java\n",
    "\n",
    "Spark needs a JVM. Check whether Java is installed.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!java -version\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Install dependencies\n",
    "\n",
    "If you are using a fresh environment, run this from a terminal:\n",
    "\n",
    "```bash\n",
    "python -m venv .venv\n",
    "source .venv/bin/activate\n",
    "pip install -r requirements.txt\n",
    "```\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pyspark.sql import SparkSession\n",
    "\n",
    "spark = SparkSession.builder \\\n    " .appName('PySpark-Setup-Check') \\\n    " .master('local[*]') \\\n    " .getOrCreate()\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Spark version:', spark.version)\n",
    "spark.stop()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Your first Spark program\n",
    "\n",
    "The SparkSession is the main entry point for DataFrame APIs and SQL.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pyspark.sql import SparkSession\n",
    "\n",
    "spark = SparkSession.builder.appName('FirstJob').master('local[*]').getOrCreate()\n",
    "\n",
    "numbers = spark.range(1, 6)\n",
    "print(numbers.collect())\n",
    "\n",
    "spark.stop()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Concept check\n",
    "\n",
    "- What is the purpose of `SparkSession`?\n",
    "- Why do we use `.master('local[*]')` for local development?\n",
    "- What is the difference between local development and cluster mode?\n",
    "\n",
    "## Next notebook\n",
    "Continue with `01_PySpark_Fundamentals.ipynb` to learn Spark architecture and lazy evaluation.\n"
   ]
  }
 ],
